- # `↯/s.106.3` — `Json.Provider.Error`
+ # `↯/s.106.3` — `Json.Provider.Error`

- Raised when a JSON value does not satisfy the schema it is being
- validated against.
+ Lançado quando um valor JSON não satisfaz o schema contra o qual está sendo validado.

- ## Cause
+ ## Causa

- Jacinta's `Json.Provider` validates JSON values against a schema as a record's fields are read,
- and reports each mismatch via this error, through the `Tactic` of the code reading the field, so
- that a validating reader can collect them all. The message is `the
- JSON was not valid according to the schema because $reason`.
+ O `Json.Provider` do Jacinta valida valores JSON contra um schema à medida que os campos de um
+ registro são lidos, e informa cada divergência por meio deste erro, pela `Tactic` do código que
+ lê o campo, para que um leitor validador possa reunir todas elas. A mensagem é
+ `the JSON was not valid according to the schema because $reason`.

- ## Variants
+ ## Variantes

- ```tabular
+ ```tabular

- column  Code
- column  Reason
- column  Meaning
- column  Message
- column  Resolution
- row  `↯/s.106.3.1`  `JsonType`  The value's type does not match what the schema requires.  `[↯/s.106.3.1] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because expected JSON type number, but found string`  Provide a value of the type the schema requires, or relax the schema if the type is genuinely flexible.
- row  `↯/s.106.3.2`  `MissingValue`  A required value is absent from the JSON. The reason names the missing field where it is known.  `[↯/s.106.3.2] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because the value of locality was missing`  Add the missing field, or mark it optional in the schema.
- row  `↯/s.106.3.3`  `IntOutOfRange`  An integer value falls outside the `minimum`/`maximum` allowed by the schema. Raised by the `"integer!"` provider type; an absent bound is `Unset` rather than a sentinel.  `[↯/s.106.3.3] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because the value was not between 1 and 99`  Constrain the value to the schema's permitted range.
- row  `↯/s.106.3.4`  `PatternMismatch`  A string value does not match the regular expression in the schema's `pattern`.  `[↯/s.106.3.4] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because the value did not conform to the regular expression [a-z]+`  Adjust the value to match the schema's pattern, or loosen the pattern.
- row  `↯/s.106.3.5`  `NumberOutOfRange`  A number falls outside the `minimum`/`maximum` (or exclusive bounds) the schema declares. Raised by the `"number!"` provider type.  `[↯/s.106.3.5] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because the number was not between -90.0 and 90.0`  Constrain the value to the schema's permitted range.
- row  `↯/s.106.3.6`  `LengthOutOfRange`  A string's length falls outside the schema's `minLength`/`maxLength`. Raised by the `"string!"` provider type.  `[↯/s.106.3.6] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because the string's length was not between 1 and 214`  Shorten or lengthen the value to fit the schema.
- row  `↯/s.106.3.7`  `NotPermitted`  A string is not one of the schema's `enum` values (or its `const`). Raised by the `"enum"` provider type.  `[↯/s.106.3.7] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because the value Polygon was not one of Point`  Use one of the listed values, or extend the schema's `enum`.
- row  `↯/s.106.3.8`  `UnexpectedKind`  A value is of a JSON kind which none of the alternatives of its union (`anyOf`, `oneOf`, or a `type` naming several) accepts.  `[↯/s.106.3.8] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because the value was a JSON boolean, which is not one of string, number`  Give a value of one of the kinds the schema lists.
- row  `↯/s.106.3.9`  `Unparsable`  A string's text is not valid for its `format`: a `json-pointer` or a `regex` which does not parse.  `[↯/s.106.3.9] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because the value a[ is not a valid regex`  Correct the value so that it parses in its format.
+ column  Código
+ column  Motivo
+ column  Significado
+ column  Mensagem
+ column  Resolução
+ row  `↯/s.106.3.1`  `JsonType`  O tipo do valor não corresponde ao que o schema exige.  `[↯/s.106.3.1] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because expected JSON type number, but found string`  Forneça um valor do tipo que o schema exige, ou relaxe o schema se o tipo for genuinamente flexível.
+ row  `↯/s.106.3.2`  `MissingValue`  Um valor obrigatório está ausente do JSON. O motivo nomeia o campo ausente quando ele é conhecido.  `[↯/s.106.3.2] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because the value of locality was missing`  Acrescente o campo ausente, ou marque-o como opcional no schema.
+ row  `↯/s.106.3.3`  `IntOutOfRange`  Um valor inteiro fica fora do `minimum`/`maximum` permitido pelo schema. Lançado pelo tipo de provedor `"integer!"`; um limite ausente é `Unset`, e não uma sentinela.  `[↯/s.106.3.3] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because the value was not between 1 and 99`  Restrinja o valor ao intervalo permitido pelo schema.
+ row  `↯/s.106.3.4`  `PatternMismatch`  Um valor string não casa com a expressão regular do `pattern` do schema.  `[↯/s.106.3.4] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because the value did not conform to the regular expression [a-z]+`  Ajuste o valor para casar com o padrão do schema, ou afrouxe o padrão.
+ row  `↯/s.106.3.5`  `NumberOutOfRange`  Um número fica fora do `minimum`/`maximum` (ou dos limites exclusivos) que o schema declara. Lançado pelo tipo de provedor `"number!"`.  `[↯/s.106.3.5] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because the number was not between -90.0 and 90.0`  Restrinja o valor ao intervalo permitido pelo schema.
+ row  `↯/s.106.3.6`  `LengthOutOfRange`  O comprimento de uma string fica fora do `minLength`/`maxLength` do schema. Lançado pelo tipo de provedor `"string!"`.  `[↯/s.106.3.6] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because the string's length was not between 1 and 214`  Encurte ou alongue o valor para que caiba no schema.
+ row  `↯/s.106.3.7`  `NotPermitted`  Uma string não é um dos valores de `enum` do schema (nem seu `const`). Lançado pelo tipo de provedor `"enum"`.  `[↯/s.106.3.7] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because the value Polygon was not one of Point`  Use um dos valores listados, ou estenda o `enum` do schema.
+ row  `↯/s.106.3.8`  `UnexpectedKind`  Um valor é de uma categoria JSON que nenhuma das alternativas de sua união (`anyOf`, `oneOf` ou um `type` que nomeia várias) aceita.  `[↯/s.106.3.8] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because the value was a JSON boolean, which is not one of string, number`  Forneça um valor de uma das categorias que o schema lista.
+ row  `↯/s.106.3.9`  `Unparsable`  O texto de uma string não é válido para seu `format`: um `json-pointer` ou uma `regex` que não pode ser analisado.  `[↯/s.106.3.9] the JSON was not valid according to the schema because the value a[ is not a valid regex`  Corrija o valor para que ele possa ser analisado em seu formato.

